  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Canicross 83, founded in 2008, brings together people who practise canicross with their dog as well as the other single-dog disciplines: canicycling, ski-joëring, canitrotte and cani-hiking. The club is affiliated with the Fédération des Sports et Loisirs Canins (FSLC) and organises group training sessions in the Var; it says it has no fenced ground, its training ground being "nature". It has members in the Var and beyond, many practitioners having no club nearby. The town of Tourves lists it among its associations.</p>
      <p>On its website the club describes canicross as a discipline that combines a dog and a human in the same effort: the dog wears a harness and is linked to its owner by an elastic towing line attached to a waist or leg belt to absorb shocks. The aim is to go fast while respecting the animal's pace; if the dog no longer wants to run or slows down, the owner must stop or slow down, and forcing the dog to run by pulling it is forbidden.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The club's website says you just need to contact it to arrange the place, day and time of a trial; it does not publish a fixed schedule, with news posted on its Facebook page. A "discovery pass" gives newcomers 3 free trial sessions, and the "first licence" offer gives a new member the last 3 months of the season. To join, fill in the club's membership form then take out the licence on the federation platform (courses.ffslc.fr); the season runs from 1 September to 31 August and the licence and membership fee are paid together to the club. The membership fee is not shown on the website. The club also organises the "Canicross en Provence Verte" race in Tourves: the latest edition announced on its website is the 16th, on Sunday 15 March 2026 at the Domaine du Château Lafoux (date now past; race entries are made on courses.ffslc.fr). The website also announces the "Canicross des Lions du Verdon" at the Les Toulons estate in Rians, with all disciplines on the programme: canicross, canicycling, canipedicycle and cani-walking.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: use the discovery pass to try the discipline before committing, and ask the club where and when the next training session takes place.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The club is active in the Var, notably in Provence Verte, with its annual race in Tourves, a village between Brignoles and Saint-Maximin-la-Sainte-Baume (town website). News and dates of upcoming events are posted on the club's Facebook page.</p>
